diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index febd4f0..28ee53c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,11 +3,64 @@
 Terraform for the reports bucket and the key the nightly export job uploads with. The job reads
 the key from `terraform output`.
 
-## Usage
+## State
+
+State lives in an S3 bucket created by `bootstrap/`. The bucket has versioning, KMS encryption,
+public access blocked, TLS-only access, and a policy that denies every principal not listed in
+`state_access_principal_arns`. Locking uses S3 native lock files (`use_lockfile`), so no DynamoDB
+table is needed. This requires Terraform 1.11 or later.
+
+State holds the uploader's secret access key in cleartext (`sensitive` only hides it from CLI
+output), so access to the bucket is access to that key. Keep the principal list short.
+
+## First-time setup (once per organisation)
+
+`bootstrap/` keeps its own state locally, because it creates the bucket the other state lives in.
+Run it from one machine with admin credentials, then keep `bootstrap/terraform.tfstate` somewhere
+safe; it is git-ignored and holds no secrets.
 
 ```sh
+cd bootstrap
 terraform init
-terraform apply
+terraform apply \
+  -var state_bucket_name=<globally-unique-bucket-name> \
+  -var 'state_access_principal_arns=["<role-or-user-arn>", ...]'
+```
+
+Include the identity running this command in the ARN list. Copy the `state_bucket_name` and
+`state_kms_key_arn` outputs into `backend.hcl` in the repository root and commit it. It holds
+only non-secret names.
+
+## Migrating the existing local state (once)
+
+On the laptop that holds `terraform.tfstate`:
+
+```sh
+terraform init -backend-config=backend.hcl -migrate-state
 ```
 
-State is kept locally in `terraform.tfstate`, so only the person who last ran `apply` has it.
+Answer `yes` to copy the local state to S3. Check with `terraform plan` (no changes expected),
+then delete the local `terraform.tfstate` and its backup files. Other engineers must not run
+`apply` until this is done.
+
+## Everyday workflow
+
+Each engineer needs AWS credentials that are in `state_access_principal_arns` and have the
+permissions this configuration manages.
+
+```sh
+terraform init -backend-config=backend.hcl
+terraform plan -out=tfplan
+terraform apply tfplan
+rm tfplan
+```
+
+Saved plans can contain secret values; they are git-ignored, so delete them after use. If a lock
+is left behind by a crashed run, remove it with `terraform force-unlock <id>` after confirming
+nobody else is running.
+
+## Recovering state
+
+The bucket is versioned. To roll back, restore a previous version of
+`reports/terraform.tfstate` in the S3 console or with `aws s3api`. Old versions expire after
+90 days.
